            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="0732" n="634" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg634"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2676: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-19T16:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 19,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>58. Your no. 32, February 2, 4 p.m.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d622-f1"/> I am assured
                    by the Foreign Office that the report of a proposed loan by Okura and Company to
                    the Chinese Government is utterly without foundation. All my investigations
                    confirm this statement of the Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
